            <h3>Trend 1: US Lawmakers Propose "AI Kill Switch Act" to Mandate=
 Emergency Shutdowns</h3>
            <p>US Representatives Ted Lieu and Nathaniel Moran have introduce=
d the "AI Kill Switch Act" (H.R. 9917) in Congress. The bipartisan bill requi=
res developers of powerful AI systems to maintain the technical capability to=
 slow down, suspend, or shut down their models.</p>
            <p>The legislation also proposes granting the Secretary of Homela=
nd Security the authority to order emergency shutdowns of AI systems posing c=
ritical risks. This reflects growing concerns that autonomous AI agents could=
 act unpredictably without human intervention mechanisms.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">Financial institutions deploying auton=
omous AI agents must prepare for strict operational resilience mandates. Comp=
liance frameworks will need to incorporate verifiable "kill switch" protocols=
 to ensure systems can be immediately deactivated during market anomalies.</p>
            <p><a href=3D"http://techtarget.itmedia.co.jp/tt/news/2608/25/new=
s10.html">Read more</a></p>

