            <h3>Trend 1: Tech Giants Call for Global Action Against AI-Powere=
d Cyberattacks</h3>
            <p>Over 100 technology companies, including OpenAI, Anthropic, Go=
ogle, and Microsoft, have signed an open letter calling for a coordinated glo=
bal effort to defend against AI-powered cyberattacks. The coalition warned of=
 a limited window to secure critical infrastructure.</p>
            <p>The letter emphasizes that increasingly capable AI models coul=
d soon automate vulnerability identification and malware generation at an unp=
recedented scale. Signatories urged governments to increase cybersecurity fun=
ding, particularly for under-resourced essential services.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">Financial institutions must treat AI-d=
riven cyber threats as a systemic risk to operational stability. Collaborativ=
e threat intelligence sharing and immediate upgrades to defensive AI security=
 protocols are essential to safeguard sensitive financial networks.</p>
